  "reason": "The current best (config_005, acc 0.650) uses rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool. The multiprofile+scvi_n200 combination showed a large gain over singleprofile (0.650 vs 0.520), confirming both are important. The key remaining uncertainty within this RNA-only direction is whether transformer aggregation outperforms avgpool for combining multiple profiles. Config_006 isolates exactly this: same encoder (scvi_n200), same multiprofile setting, only aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer. This is a clean single-variable comparison that will tell us which aggregation to carry forward into multimodal experiments. Under the 5-experiment budget remaining, resolving the aggregation choice now prevents wasting slots on suboptimal aggregation in later multimodal trials, making it the highest-information next step."
}

